      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ given below have a discontinuity at $x=-2?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{x+2}, & x<-2 \\\\ \\frac{2}{x+2}, & x>-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's check the conditions necessary for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-2.$\n\n- We have that $f(-2)$ is not defined since $x=-2$ does not belong to the domain of $f(x).$ $\\times $\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-2$ because $f(-2)$ does not exist.",
